# Accepted Trivy findings. Every entry needs a reason and a review date.
# Used by the backend image scan in .github/workflows/backend-ci.yml.

# SixLabors.ImageSharp 3.1.11 (reviewed 2026-10-18)
# These are fixed only in ImageSharp 4.x, which fails the build without a paid
# Six Labors license key. There is no patched 3.x release.
# The only use of the library is src/backend/Infrastructure/Imaging/PerceptualHashService.cs,
# which allow-lists JPEG/PNG/WebP, loads the image and calls Resize. So:
#   - the TIFF encoder bugs are not reachable: nothing is ever encoded, and TIFF is rejected
#     before Load
#   - the HistogramEqualization bug is not reachable: only Resize is used
# Revisit if a license is obtained (upgrade to >= 4.1.2 and delete these lines), or if the
# library is used for anything beyond decoding uploaded JPEG/PNG/WebP.
CVE-2026-106110
CVE-2026-106113
CVE-2026-106115